# Real Images Only (Cursor mirror of rules/09-real-images.md)

> Canonical source: `rules/09-real-images.md`. If they differ, canonical wins.

Use **real images** from these two sources — never AI-generated imagery:

1. Unsplash — https://unsplash.com (hero, product, backgrounds, avatars)
2. Pinterest — https://www.pinterest.com (moodboard, lifestyle, niche imagery)

Rules:

- Copy the EXACT image URL from the source (`images.unsplash.com/photo-…`, `i.pinimg.com/…`). Never guess or construct an ID.
- Unsplash sizing params: `?w=1600&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop`.
- VERIFY every URL before shipping: HTTP 200, image content-type, expected dimensions.
- Attribution: photographer/source in `CREDITS.md` or a comment.
- Integrate via the framework's image component (e.g. `next/image`) — verify props in docs, never guess. Meaningful alt text on every image.
- Generated images ONLY when the user explicitly asks (then label them as generated).
- No placeholder services (picsum, via.placeholder, grey boxes) in final builds.
- Other stock sites need user approval via `rules/07-how-to-add-a-rule.md`.
